# slash local configuration.
# Copy this to .env (which is gitignored) and adjust the values, or just run
# `go run .` once interactively — on first run it offers to create .env for you.

# Local clone of the target repo, used for all git/worktree operations.
# A leading ~ is expanded to your home directory. Default: ~/dev/plug-and-pay
SLASH_REPO_DIR=~/dev/plug-and-pay

# SQLite DB path (default data/graph.db)
# SLASH_DB=data/graph.db

# Jira notification feed (the bell menu shown on /pr-overview). Needs an
# Atlassian API token (id.atlassian.com → Security → API tokens); without one
# the feed stays empty and nothing is fetched. Deliberately env vars and NOT
# data/settings.json — that file is served to the browser by GET /api/settings.
# These three can also be filled in from the settings page's "Inloggegevens"
# row, which writes them here through the app_settings workflow and applies
# them immediately (see .claude/docs/settings-page.md).
# SLASH_JIRA_EMAIL=you@example.com
# SLASH_JIRA_TOKEN=your-atlassian-api-token
# SLASH_JIRA_SITE=plugandpaybv.atlassian.net

# Offline/test toggles — set to "off" to avoid touching the network.
# SLASH_GITHUB=off
# SLASH_CLAUDE=off
# SLASH_JIRA=off
